From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:04:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot: limit the eMMC
 to 26MHz

After a cold boot, U-Boot often cannot read the eMMC on the ODROID-GO
Ultra (Samsung AJTD4R). In the 52MHz high speed mode the 8-bit bus test
fails, U-Boot falls back to a 1-bit bus at 40MHz, and every read then
fails, so distro boot finds no partition table on mmc 1 and the board
cannot boot from the eMMC. On my board it failed on 3 of 3 cold boots
with a UART cable attached, and on 1 of 3 without one.

At the same U-Boot prompt, reinitializing the eMMC at 26MHz gives an
8-bit bus and the reads work. The meson MMC driver has no tuning in
U-Boot, while Linux tunes the eMMC and runs it in HS200 without
problems.

Limit the eMMC to 26MHz in U-Boot. With this change the board booted
from the eMMC on 15 of 15 cold boots (10 with a UART cable, 5 without).
Linux is not affected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
index 9ae0a50..a8a7693 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -30,3 +30,13 @@
 &vddio_c {
 	regulator-init-microvolt = <3300000>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * After a cold boot, U-Boot sometimes cannot use the eMMC at 52MHz: the
+ * 8-bit bus test fails, it falls back to a 1-bit bus, and reads then fail,
+ * so the board cannot boot from the eMMC. This controller has no tuning in
+ * U-Boot; at 26MHz the 8-bit bus works.
+ */
+&sd_emmc_c {
+	max-frequency = <26000000>;
+};
